{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5120-1","published":"2026-11-05T12:19:29Z","modified":"2026-11-06T12:30:03.490751417Z","related":["CVE-2026-110752","CVE-2026-110754","CVE-2026-110755","CVE-2026-110756","CVE-2026-110757","CVE-2026-110758","CVE-2026-110759"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-110752","CVE-2026-110754","CVE-2026-110755","CVE-2026-110756","CVE-2026-110757","CVE-2026-110758","CVE-2026-110759"],"summary":"Security update for perl-Text-CSV_XS","details":"This update for perl-Text-CSV_XS fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-110752: unclamped RFC 7111 selector range pre-allocation in fragment() can cause memory exhaustion via large\n  index ranges (bsc#1286138).\n- CVE-2026-110754: unfreed field array memory leak on getline() syntax errors can lead to process memory exhaustion via\n  malformed CSV input (bsc#1286188).\n- CVE-2026-110755: quadratic buffer copying overhead during CR-only line parsing in getline() can cause CPU exhaustion\n  and denial of service (bsc#1286198).\n- CVE-2026-110756: invalid UTF-8 bytes during buffer flushes in print() can cause silent field truncation (bsc#1286130).\n- CVE-2026-110757: unquoted writing of numeric-flagged strings containing newlines in combine() and print() can cause\n  record splitting and row injection (bsc#1286191).\n- CVE-2026-110758: missing buffer start boundary check in strip_trail_whitespace under allow_whitespace can cause heap\n  out-of-bounds read and memory corruption (bsc#1286137).\n- CVE-2026-110759: improper end-of-file marker handling after a lone CR can cause Text::CSV_XS to inject an unexpected\n  0xFF byte (bsc#1286128).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"perl-Text-CSV_XS","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Module for Development Tools 15 SP7","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/perl-Text-CSV_XS&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Module%20for%20Development%20Tools%2015%20SP7"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.34-150000.3.6.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"pe